OneiOS take18, userland/metal/patches/metal2vulkan/0002: the opaque rasterization rate map buffer is reflected.
Upstream: Droid-VM/macOS-DroidVM a80044a (lateautumn233, 2026-11-13: patches/metal2vulkan-macos/0003), the same change as
Droid-VM/UniXNU wip/hackintosh patches/metal2vulkan/0040-rate-map-buffer-reflection.patch (on 555b13d5); its two hunks apply
to this stack unchanged.
What: a pipeline argument of type metal::rasterization_rate_map_data (no member layout in AIR) is reflected as a struct of
the runtime's parameter data size and alignment (RasterizationRateMap::PARAMETER_DATA_SIZE/_ALIGNMENT) instead of refusing
the whole pipeline's reflection.
Why: a client that asks reflection of such a pipeline got none (the pipeline refused with it).
Switch: none (a reflection answer that was a refusal). Removable: yes (ONEIOS_METAL_SKIP=rate-map-buffer-reflection).

